---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import IntakeForm from '../components/IntakeForm.astro';
import { usImmigrationStatusField } from '../lib/intake-context';
import HeroBanner from '../components/HeroBanner.astro';
import RequirementsIntakeCta from '../components/RequirementsIntakeCta.astro';

const title = 'Portugal HQA Visa for Americans - US Tax and Route Fit';
const metaTitle = `${title} | Portugal HQA Residency`;
const metaDescription =
  'Portugal HQA visa for Americans in 2026 still turns on a Portuguese host and role. US tax residency rules stay in force; compare routes before you file.';
---

<Layout title={metaTitle} description={metaDescription}>
  <article>
    <header>
      <HeroBanner
        image="/images/portugal-hqa-visa-for-americans.jpg"
        alt="Stone statue of a man in sixteenth-century dress on a paved terrace, with hills and a cable-stayed bridge beyond"
        title={title}
        items={[
          { href: '/', label: 'Home' },
          { href: '/portugal-hqa-visa', label: 'Portugal HQA Visa' },
          { label: 'For Americans' },
        ]}
        position="object-[center_42%] sm:object-[center_40%] lg:object-[center_38%]"
      />
      <div class="bg-background">
        <div class="site-container py-24 md:py-32">
        <p class="max-w-3xl">
          Portugal HQA visa for Americans is the same highly qualified activity residence heading that applies to other non-EU nationals: a qualifying role and a Portuguese host. US citizenship does not create a separate HQA product. What is US-specific is tax, reporting, and the temptation to treat a capital route or a passive-income permit as interchangeable with this file. US tax issues are on
          <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-tax" class="inline-link">HQA visa tax</a>.
          Capital tickets are compared on
          <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-vs-golden-visa" class="inline-link">HQA visa vs Golden Visa</a>.
        </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="bg-background-alt">
      <div class="site-container max-w-3xl py-24 md:py-32">
        <section>
          <h2>The host test does not change for a US passport</h2>
          <p class="mt-6">
            ESTA and a tourist stay are not this permit. A remote US employment contract with no Portuguese host is a different analysis. The role and host tests sit on
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-requirements" class="inline-link">HQA visa requirements</a>
            and
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-eligibility" class="inline-link">HQA visa eligibility</a>.
            If the household’s plan is funds in Portugal rather than a highly qualified post, the Golden Visa comparison is the right page. If the plan is foreign passive income without a Portuguese role, use
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-vs-d7" class="inline-link">HQA visa vs D7</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-24">
          <h2>US tax does not end when you receive a Portuguese card</h2>
          <p class="mt-6">
            The United States taxes on citizenship and on US tax residency. A Portuguese residence card does not cancel that. Worldwide income, foreign-account reporting, and any applicable US–Portugal treaty or totalization questions belong with a US-qualified tax professional and, where Portuguese tax residency also attaches, with Portuguese tax counsel. This site does not compute a US return. See
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-tax" class="inline-link">HQA visa tax</a>
            for the Portuguese-residency side only.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>

    <RequirementsIntakeCta
      source="/portugal-hqa-visa-for-americans"
      image="/images/portugal-hqa-visa-for-americans-cta-divider.jpg"
      alt="Lisbon terrace and river used on the HQA visa for Americans page"
      heading="Match a US file to the Portuguese host and tax overlay"
      copy="Not sure how the host test and US tax residency sit together? Enter your details and our advisory team can help point you in the right direction."
    />

    <div class="bg-background-alt">
      <div class="site-container max-w-3xl py-24 md:py-32">
        <section>
          <h2>How Americans usually move the file</h2>
          <p class="mt-6">
            Lodging is still the
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-application" class="inline-link">HQA visa application</a>
            sequence. Budget state fees and professional work on
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-cost" class="inline-link">HQA visa cost</a>.
            Family members follow
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-family" class="inline-link">HQA visa family</a>.
            H-1B professionals considering Portuguese residency should also read
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-for-h1b-holders" class="inline-link">Portugal HQA Visa for H-1B holders</a>.
            The program overview is the
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa" class="inline-link">Portugal HQA visa</a>
            guide.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="bg-cta-tint">
      <div class="site-container flex flex-col items-start gap-6 py-24 md:py-32">
        <h2 class="max-w-3xl">Separate the Portuguese host file from the US tax file</h2>
        <p class="max-w-2xl">
          This page is informational. It is not legal, tax, or immigration advice. US and Portuguese tax rules both apply until a qualified professional says otherwise for your facts.
        </p>
        {/* TODO: no backend yet */}
        <IntakeForm source="/portugal-hqa-visa-for-americans" contextField={usImmigrationStatusField} />
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
